KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ non-template constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ constructor template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.base.init]/9.3, /13: a constructor default-initializes the
bases its mem-initializer-list does not name.  typecheck_compound_body
completes the list of non-template constructors
(full_member_initialization); a constructor template's specialization
never gets it, so leaf's user-provided default constructor is not called
and t.value is nondeterministic (also bin53).  Calling
full_member_initialization in instantiate_template was tried (round 163w)
and double-initialized: mem-initializer pack expansions (`leaf<I, T>(u)...')
are expanded later, when the method body is converted.  Found while
reducing libc++'s __tuple_impl.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
